## 1. Parameter snapshot

Freeze these values before an exam. Change them only during group creation or a
major adjustment window, and always leave a record.

| Parameter | Value | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Review units | inherit (protocol default 2; legal values 0/1/2) | `10_student/profile/profile.md` |
| Pass mark | inherit (final 60 / resit 1: 60 / resit 2: 50) | `exam_protocol.md` §9 |
| Time multiplier | inherit (quiz ×2.0 / final ×1.2 / resit ×1.5) | `exam_protocol.md` §9 |
| Grade weighting | written paper 70% / process indicators 30% | `course_group_rules.md` §3 |

## 2. Settlement-gate state

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Exam debt status | `open` |
| Sittings used | 0 |
| Next sitting | — (await trigger: quiz by group calendar; final by calendar + scope gate) |
| Review units used | 0 |

Legal exam-debt states: `open` / `in_remediation` / `settled` / `archived`.

- `settled`: the pass mark was reached; the debt exits.
- `archived`: resit 2 still failed; record the course as not passed and close it,
  updating the lifecycle in `progress.md`.
- Re-entry after either exit requires opening a course retake: return the lifecycle
  to active, schedule a new cycle, use a fresh assessment paper, and retain the
  existing mistake bank (`exam_protocol.md` §10).

